From 89bbae68495e856661ba9b5c93a8359570ea3ba9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:12:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] fix(#95): the open-line census is read directly or
 named absent, and FAULT_OPEN is empty
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The defect, verbatim from the issue: "an object that never carried the flag reads clean." Fourteen sites
read `missing_line_standings`, `not_consulted` and `not_consulted_dynamic` with a default of `()` / `0`:
"every open line has a standing; no test was left unconsulted; no test dispatches by a name the static
route cannot follow". The last is the dangerous one: it decides whether a line no test runs is called
`unexecuted` (write a test from an input) or `unconsulted` (a test may already run it).

Why the obvious fix is wrong: the first two are declared by ConvergeResult / SuiteAudit / SurvivorReport
and are read DIRECTLY. `not_consulted_dynamic` on a PROFILE is different: Detective stashes it after
routing, so a profile `profile` never routed, and a verdict-cache row written before the census existed,
genuinely lack it. There the old `()` was a clean answer to a question nobody answered. Now
`audit.dynamic_census` (pure) maps an absent census to the single named entry `absent:not_consulted_dynamic`,
`profile_dynamic_census` reads the stash three-valued, `missing_line_standing` therefore says `unconsulted`
for a line nothing runs, and the page row reads "could not determine which tests ... this measurement
carries no census of them". The verdict cache stores no key for an absent census and restores none, where
the round trip used to turn absence into an empty census.

States of `dynamic_census`: None -> ["absent:not_consulted_dynamic"] (no census was taken); a list,
empty or not, is a census that was taken and is returned as it is.

FAULT_OPEN is now {} and `test_the_fault_registry_is_empty_and_says_so` says so; the standing guard still
fails any new clean-default read of a fault flag. Doubles of the result types gain the fields across tests/.

Not closed: the typing.Protocols for the duck-typed results (a later commit in this lane). Pin of
`audit.py::dynamic_census`: the run did not reach COMPLETE; final line "Incomplete: 1 killable (no value
pin) · 5/6 killed · minimal cover 1 test(s)" (observed `([],)`: real [] vs mutant ['absent:...']); not
ground further, the integrator re-pins. test_absorbed_rename_intent's `test_no_registry_entry_names_
something_the_pair_now_declares` fails on the current Wesker integration tree (it now declares `bound`),
independent of this lane.

Disarmed, 3 of 3 new census tests fail. 832 neighbour tests pass under 3.14 and 3.12 apart from that one
guard; ruff clean under pinned 0.16.7.
